\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Volume within a constrained field space}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{A linear constraint on the [real field space](fdip-002C) leaves
a subspace with the inherited inner product. Its orthonormal coordinates
are not generally a subset of the original site coordinates. The
isometry result \ref{fdip-002L} compares the coordinate volumes supplied
by such choices. What measure on the subspace is specified by requiring
all of those orthonormal coordinates to preserve volume?}
